          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-19T03:15:00.546Z",
          "html": "<p>Got it. When you hand over the components (column mode for <code>&lt;ui-tree&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;ui-graph&gt;</code>), P1 brings them in onto <code>main</code>'s column view. No netlist code or netlist files come across. Every netlist step works from a small made-up example, never real netlist data. The plans are being changed to match.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c2": {
      "anchor": "p-file-upload-in-spell",
      "kind": "phase",
      "label": "File Upload In Spell",
      "excerpt": "File Upload In Spell",
      "text": "lets add a `destination` URL attr for where the results would be posted, and an `action` for spell action to invoke instead.\n\nAlso, size limit, max file count.  Anything else that uploader thingers usually show?  What would the UI look like for this?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-19T23:26:14.665Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-19T23:28:08.310Z",
          "html": "<p>P9's plan is rewritten: <code>upload</code> is now two attributes, <code>destination</code> (a URL each file is posted to) and <code>action</code> (a Spell action called with the files instead). Both set: the action wins and a warning is logged. Neither: the files are only held and listed, and <code>ui-upload</code> still fires first, so a handler can take any upload over.</p>\n<p>Added <code>max-size</code> and <code>max-files</code>, and the plan now says what it looks like: a drop area with a Choose files button and the limits, then a row per file with its size, a progress bar, a tick or the reason it failed, and an ✕.</p>\n<p>One clash to know: in plain HTML a form's <code>action</code> is the URL it posts to, and <code>&lt;ui-input&gt;</code>'s <code>action</code> places its joined buttons. The plan keeps your name and says in the docs that it's a Spell action, not a URL.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-19T23:26:31.712Z"
      }
    }
  },
  "on": {}
